A||||3||Ozzy||Simply Speakers||||
Z||000000||Ozzy||08-07-99||01:19 PM||||Hey folks...<p>I guess there are several manufacturers that make a 4" x 10" replacement for the dash mounts but if you are looking for a quick good sounding fix for your shot originals the Kenwoods I bought from "The Good Guys" for $89.00 worked just fine. I will upgrade the stereo eventually to something that will be somewhat beefier but for now these work great!
Z||000001||Bruce||08-08-99||08:05 PM||||All thumbs, here! Was the installation simple? I bought a great radio (thanks, Gregg), but I feel the stock speakers lack clarity.
Z||000002||Ozzy||08-08-99||09:41 PM||||Hey Bruce...<p>Yeah...It can't get a lot simpler really. The mounting holes were a little off compared to the factory jobs but with a little fenageling I managed to locate them in the same positions. The connectors (vehicle factory connectors) did not match up to the replacements I purchased so I simply cut a small section from each of the pre-terminated leads supplied with the replacement speakers and spliced them to the car speaker wires. There were no polarity markings on the old speakers so heres how I checked that out...<p>Mark or remember what color existing wire goes to both left and right speakers each in turn. Then take the old speaker and find a 1.5v AA battery or similar and a small piece of jumper wire. Hold one bare end of the jumper on the negative end of the battery. Attatch or hold the other bare end of the jumper to one of the old speaker terminals. Now momentarily touch the positive term. of the battery to the other speaker term. If the cone moves outward then the positive term. of the battery is touching the positive term of the speaker. If the cone moves inward the the opposite is true. Now that you know which terminals on the old speakers were positive (assuming the factory wiring was correct) splice the color according to the old configuration. This will ensure that your new speakers will be wired 'in phase'.<p>Ozzy
Z||000003||fierosound||11-26-1999||01:34 PM||||Just wondering....<BR>What size speakers are used in the seats?  Are they 3 inch diameter?  I came across some in a local Auto Stereo shop and thought they may fit Fiero seats.<BR>I've mounted one as a center channel in may car, and the sound it produces is really quite good.||||reg||5
